# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Build output. The quickstart builds ./re0auth at the repository root, and
# `make release` writes dist/. Anchored so these cannot shadow an unrelated
# directory of the same name deeper in the tree (internal/webui/dist is the
# embedded frontend, and has its own rules).
/re0auth
/referencesource
/dist/

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Local performance report outputs (make perf); in CI they live in artifacts
/bench.txt
/load.txt
/report.md

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# local configuration and secrets
config/*.local.*
config/*.secret.*
*.local.toml
# The default config path. It holds deployment-specific settings and may name the
# environment variables holding secrets, so it must never be committed. (The
# example file already tells operators it is ignored; this makes that true.)
config/re0auth.toml

# The backup scripts' default output (scripts/backup.sh:12, backup-keys.sh:23):
# plaintext SQL dumps and a KEK/OIDC/audit-key .env. A `git add -A` in the
# documented backup workflow must not stage them, so the rule covers the default
# directory and both file shapes wherever an operator points the scripts.
/backups/
*.dump
*.env
# The .dump files under _audit/scriptprobe/ are checked in deliberately (the
# backup-script probes read them as fixtures), so re-include them; the rules
# above are about backup output, not about test data.
!_audit/scriptprobe/**

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Never commit third-party documents (papers, PDFs): redistribution rights are
# usually not ours, and they bloat the repository. Link instead.
docs/*.pdf
*.pdf

# IDE CLI
.commandcode

# The audit workspace. Audits run here — throwaway probes, generated binaries,
# machine-local notes and the shared brief the area agents read. What belongs in
# the repository is archived next to the report it backs: the fifth round's raw
# records are under docs/audit-5/, and the tests that fail on its findings are
# under internal/zzprobe/. Anchored so it cannot shadow a deeper directory of the
# same name.
/scratchpad/
